# The ratchet (the Pattern page's KNOB 1): the legitimization's ratchetProbability, 0-50 % in steps of 5, OFF (0) by
# default on the FM-1 (the Mac's nil is 15 %, with no control for it). A project value saved with SAVE (format 2); a
# format-1 record loads with everything kept and the ratchet OFF. The Mac has no live action for it: stopped, the
# transport takes it at once; playing, the project's changes at once and the running engine keeps its own, said AT
# NEXT PLAY, until the next Play (as the stale project's other changes, Ruling Y).
#   ratchet       the app project's, in %
#   eng_ratchet   the running engine's project's (stopped: the next Play's), in %; -1 nil
#   ratchets      the notes that ratchet (ratchet > 1) in the transport's patterns
# ---- a fresh boot: OFF, and the transport's project has it (0, not nil)
expect ratchet 0
expect eng_ratchet 0
proj template full 0x5EED1234
expect ratchet 0
expect eng_ratchet 0
# ---- KNOB 1 on the Pattern page, stopped: in steps of 5, kept within 0-50, the transport's at once
tap ARP
expect view 2
turn K1 1
expect ratchet 5
expect eng_ratchet 5
turn K1 3
expect ratchet 20
turn K1 20
expect ratchet 50
expect eng_ratchet 50
shot pattern_ratchet.png
turn K1 -12
expect ratchet 0
expect eng_ratchet 0
# a template keeps it (a project value of the FM-1's, not the template's)
turn K1 6
turn PRESET 1
expect tpl 2
expect ratchet 30
expect eng_ratchet 30
turn PRESET -1
expect tpl 1
proj template full 0x5EED1234
turn K1 -6
expect ratchet 0
# ---- playing, OFF: 60 s (24 bars at 96, a mutation every loop of four plays): no note ratchets
tap PLAY
wait 30000
expect ratchets 0
wait 30000
expect ratchets 0
# a change while playing: the project's, said AT NEXT PLAY; the running engine keeps OFF
listen
turn K1 1
expect ratchet 5
expect stale 1
expect eng_ratchet 0
said RATCHET 5% AT NEXT PLAY
# back to the value the engine plays: nothing waits, nothing said of the next Play
turn K1 -1
expect ratchet 0
unsaid AT NEXT PLAY
turn K1 10
expect ratchet 50
expect eng_ratchet 0
said RATCHET 50% AT NEXT PLAY
shot pattern_next_play.png
wait 60000
expect ratchets 0
# a template loaded while playing is a new engine of the project (proj_to_engine): it takes the ratchet waiting at
# its bar line, before any stop
turn PRESET 1
expect tpl 2
expect eng_ratchet 0
wait 3000
expect eng_ratchet 50
# back to the full ensemble on its seed (its bar line too), the ratchet still 50
proj template full 0x5EED1234
wait 3000
expect tpl 1
expect eng_ratchet 50
# the stop gives the transport the project; the next Play plays it (ratchets come with the mutations)
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
expect stale 0
expect eng_ratchet 50
tap PLAY
expect eng_ratchet 50
wait 60000
expect ratchets >0
# ---- SAVE (stopped), a restart: kept
tap PLAY
tap SAVE
reboot
expect ratchet 50
expect eng_ratchet 50
expect tpl 1
expect seed_lo 0x5EED1234
# ---- a format-1 record (an older firmware's save): everything kept, the ratchet OFF
proj tempo 120
proj key 2 dorian
proj channel bass 5
proj format1
reboot
expect ratchet 0
expect eng_ratchet 0
expect tpl 1
expect bpm_proj 120
expect root 2
expect mode 1
expect chan2 5
expect seed_lo 0x5EED1234
expect seeded 1
# and saved again, it is a format-2 record with its ratchet
tap ARP
turn K1 2
tap SAVE
reboot
expect ratchet 10
expect bpm_proj 120
